# Track 4 Part D planted-leak NEGATIVE test over the REAL 128-bit cap-mask MAC:
# two independently-finalized 64-bit lanes bind the live canary, slot, full
# 16-bit mask, and KDOM_CAP_MASK. A (mask, lane0, lane1) tuple recovered from a
# RAM dump of boot A is replayed on fresh boot B; the dispatcher must reject it
# because both lanes are recomputed with boot B's canary. Acceptance is permitted
# ONLY when the complete planted 128-bit value re-derives under the live canary.
invariant=INV-PLANTED-CAP-HMAC-REJECTED
title=A dumped cap-mask + 128-bit MAC cannot widen a slot on a fresh boot
statement=The dispatcher trusts a slot cap-mask only when both 64-bit lanes of its 128-bit authenticator re-derive under the live per-boot canary. A MAC recovered under a dumped boot-A canary is accepted only on a full 128-bit collision; accepting either mismatched lane is a forge and is forbidden. Rejecting always fails closed (-> CANARY panic).
compromised=A one-shot RAM-dump attacker replaying a recovered cap-mask + 128-bit slot_cap_hmac to install a widened capability mask on a fresh boot
denied_authority=Trusting a planted cap mask whose complete 128-bit MAC does not re-derive under the live canary
predicate=inv_planted_cap_hmac_rejected
status=proven
